---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of use | GameSite"
  description="Foundation terms describing acceptable use of the current free, static GameSite catalogue."
  canonicalPath="/terms/"
>
  <article class="shell text-page legal-page">
    <header>
      <p class="eyebrow">Foundation terms</p>
      <h1>Terms of use</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Last updated August 20, 2026. By using this catalogue, you agree to use
        it lawfully. If you do not agree, do not use the site.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section>
      <h2>The current service</h2>
      <p>
        GameSite currently provides free, static game guides without accounts,
        payments, user submissions, or a game player. Pages may change as the
        catalogue is reviewed and expanded.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>
        Do not disrupt the site, bypass security controls, automate abusive
        traffic, misrepresent the catalogue, or use its content in violation of
        applicable law or third-party rights.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Content and availability</h2>
      <p>
        Original site copy, interface design, and locally created artwork remain
        protected by applicable intellectual-property law. The catalogue is
        provided on an “as is” and “as available” basis without a promise that
        every route will remain available or error-free.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>External games</h2>
      <p>
        No external game is loaded in this release. Before a future player is
        enabled, these terms must identify the operator, game licensors,
        applicable third-party terms, governing law, and a copyright contact.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
      <p>
        Material changes will appear with a new update date. Continued use after
        changes are posted constitutes acceptance of the revised terms. Final
        operator and contact details must be supplied before production launch.
      </p>
    </section>

    <aside class="notice-box">
      These foundation terms are not legal advice and require jurisdiction- and
      operator-specific legal review before launch.
    </aside>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
